  "expect": {
    "branches": [
      "Filter Out Upcoming keeps 2 of 3"
    ],
    "offline": "In n8n's v1 order the playlist lookup branch (higher on the canvas) runs first: the PlaylistId tab still holds yesterday's id, which Delete Old Playlist removes; then the new playlist is created, its id saved to that row (update matching Playlist Group), the channels read, each channel searched for the last day's videos, upcoming broadcasts filtered out, each video added and a Telegram message sent per added video. The search sends channel_id (not YouTube's documented channelId) and the template's placeholder key; answered per channel in call order as the template's author saw it. YouTube's playlists.delete is sent with the id in a JSON body, not the query; answered 204 as the node's users see it. The Telegram chat id is empty in the template; the overlay fills it on both sides. The workflow's timezone is Asia/Manila."
  }
